Not too much this week, though those of you who've been having trouble
with either segfaults or the monsndx[] panic will be happy; I found the
cause of that and cleaned it up, so things should be better now.  Any
games that had crashed have been restored as of 10am UTC-4 today.

The wish tracker is the only major "new" thing this week; it doesn't
push stuff into individual dumplogs yet, but if nothing else it will
allow even someone who's local to track what they're wishing for at any
given time.

Also, we are now at a new domain: sporkhack.com.  The old addresses are 
still valid, but this one is both shorter and (hopefully) easier to 
remember.  Windows binaries will show up sometime later tonight, unless
yacc decides to be a pill again.

I'm not going to break save next weekend, but I am (hopefully) going to 
start pushing some more major balance changes in over the next month while 
devnull's going on and traffic slows down for me a bit.  It would be an 
excellent idea to keep an eye on the changelog if you haven't played in 
a few days, just in case, say, the intrinsic stuff shows up?  ;)

Speaking of changelog...

--------------
10/28:
* Bug fix: segfault causing crashes found and removed
-- This should also fix the monsndx[] panics, since those were 
   occurring in the same piece of code
* Wishtracker's information order reordered slightly

10/26:
* Bug fix: new bag type now #lootable
* Wishtracker now reports 1st, 2nd, 3rd, etc. wish (per game)

10/25:
* Wield-on-fire order changed so selected launcher is wielded before 
  autoquiver is called; this allows autoquiver to correctly pick ammo
* Some enhancements to Forkney's !whereis (#sporkhack only)

10/24:
* Wish tracker implemented.  All wishes will be logged to a wishtracker 
  file in the playground with game turn, player name, and the string of 
  what was wished for.
-- Forkney in #sporkhack now announces wishes in real-time, of course.

10/23:
* Windows binaries available!
* Role init cleanup/bug fixes: 
-- Quiverable objects should start in player's quiver.
-- Launchers should start as "chosen ranged weapon".
-- Other weapons should be assigned primary/alternate weapon slots as 
   appropriate.
* Rogue's starting weapon changed to stiletto instead of shortsword in 
  burst of whimsy

